ps grant for each applicant (if eligible) for approval by the School Dean. This AIT Scholarship grant can only be awarded once before enrollment and cannot be changed during the entire study period.

Interested applicants can apply through the AITonline admissionportal. No separate application to fill out. Applicants may describe in their statement of purpose seeking this scholarship. This can be in a separate file and uploaded to the application portal.

Eligibility

* All nationalities;
* Meeting AIT’s English Proficiency Requirement (i.e. IELTS-Academic or AIT EET score of 5.0 or above for Master’s and 5.5 for Doctoral program);
* Having a four‐year Bachelor’s degree from a recognized university;
* Having a master’s degree from a recognized university for Ph.D. applicants and should have a Cumulative GPA of 3.50 in their Master’s degree and 2.75 in their undergraduate program from top universities.

Deadline for August 2026 Intake: 15  July 2026

Contact:AIT Admissions OfficeTel: 02

